GREEN FUTURE FOUNDATION
About Our Organization

================================================================================
OUR MISSION
================================================================================

Green Future Foundation is dedicated to environmental education and conservation
in the Pacific Northwest. We believe that by connecting people—especially young
people—with nature, we can inspire the next generation of environmental stewards.

Founded in 2015 by Dr. Emily Carter, we have grown from a small volunteer group
meeting in a church basement to an organization serving over 10,000 students
annually through our award-winning educational programs.

================================================================================
LEADERSHIP TEAM
================================================================================

EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR: Dr. Emily Carter

Dr. Carter founded Green Future Foundation after 15 years as a biology professor
at University of Washington. Frustrated that environmental education was being
cut from school budgets, she started bringing nature education directly to
classrooms.

Education:
- PhD in Environmental Science, Stanford University (2000)
- MS in Biology, UC Berkeley (1996)
- BS in Environmental Studies, University of Oregon (1994)

Recognition:
- Seattle Business Journal "40 Under 40" (2017)
- Washington State Environmental Excellence Award (2022)

